#version 450
/*==============================================================================================================================================
                                                          SURFELGRIDCLEAR.COMP
==============================================================================================================================================*/
// 🧩 Pass 1 of the per-frame grid build: zero the per-cell Offsets header. The count pass then atomicAdds into it, the scan turns the counts into END
//    offsets, and the slot pass atomic-decrements them while writing the list. Every cell's offset MUST start at 0 each frame or last frame's counts
//    leak into this frame's prefix sum.
//
//    🔴 Ported 1:1 from webgiya surfelHashGrid.ts:370-377 (computeClear), which clears the [0, totalCells] header of the merged buffer. Here the buffer
//       is SPLIT (F6): this clears the standalone Offsets SSBO. The List SSBO is init to -1 ONCE at buffer creation (host side) and left alone per frame —
//       the slot pass overwrites exactly the entries the count/scan allocated, so a per-frame list clear is unnecessary and webgiya skips it too.
//
//    🔴 The element count is a COMPILE-TIME CONSTANT (SURFEL_TOTAL_CELLS + 1, the per-cell header plus the terminal grand-total entry), NOT a push field.
//       This pass shares the ONE slotting push block (SurfelSlottingConstants: vec4 CameraPosition @0, vec4 GridOrigin @16, ...) with count/slot. A lone
//       `int ElementCount` here would alias offset 0 = CameraPosition.x, so the guard would read floatBitsToInt(camera.x) — a garbage huge int that lets
//       lanes past the buffer write OUT OF BOUNDS into whatever allocation follows Offsets, corrupting it nondeterministically across frames.

#include "SurfelGrid.glsl"

layout(local_size_x = 256) in;

layout(std430, binding = 0) buffer OffsetsBuffer { int Offsets[]; };

void main()
{
    uint Index = gl_GlobalInvocationID.x;
    if (Index < SURFEL_TOTAL_CELLS + 1u)       // 262144 per-cell entries + 1 terminal grand-total entry
        Offsets[Index] = 0;
}
